From: =?UTF-8?q?=E9=AB=98=E5=BA=86=E4=B8=B0?= <gao.qingfeng@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:36:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/29] perf(fuse): readdirplus batch-fetches child attrs
 instead of serial stat

Closes #15 (gqf2008/brewfs)

readdirplus issued one stat_ino per entry (N cache lookups / backend
round-trips), dominating latency on large directories.

- MetaLayer::batch_stat default (sequential stat) + MetaClient override
  that serves cache hits from memory and batches cold misses through
  store.batch_stat (Redis MGET).
- VFS::stat_inos: batched attr fetch with close-to-open size overlay and
  per-inode fallback on error.
- readdirplus uses one stat_inos call for all child entries.
- Tests: SQLite client returns attrs in input order (missing -> None);
  Redis client batches 4 cold misses into one MGET and serves a fully
  warm batch with zero Redis traffic.
